{
  "_doc": "Toon ramps for the world (castle cells, rooms, kit) in the client's ToonRamp format (client/src/game/toon/palette.ts WORLD_TOON; docs/art/style-guide.md). Each row is a partial ToonRamp over the client's BASE_RAMP: shadowTint = sRGB multiplier of the shadow band (warm, saturated, never grey); threshold = n.l where the lit band is half on (-1..1, 0 = terminator, -1 = always lit); softness = half-width of the step in n.l; shadowLight = share of direct light the shadow band keeps; rim, specular, saturation (extra in the shadow band), outline (0 none .. 1 silhouettes and creases), farStart / farEnd (metres from the camera over which the key's step softens and rim and highlight fade: far rib facets; 0 = off). Lookup: exact material name, then the longest key ending in '*' that prefixes it, then 'default'. Castle D1 (docs/art/castle-kit.md), world shade fields: shadeShift = how far the baked shade x (COLOR_0 r = g = b, 0.35 deepest corner .. 1 open) moves the key's threshold, so corners fall into the tinted shadow band; aoFloor = fill kept at x = 0.35..0 (mix(aoFloor, 1, x)); valueFloor = colour kept likewise (some darkening where the key is weak); skyLift = fill by normal (1 + skyLift * n.y), and on a row with skyLift the hemisphere's ground colour gives way to the sky's hue (undersides darker, never the brown bounce); rimWidth = set on a row, it takes the characters' rim (both bands, brighter lit); nearFade = [near, far] metres from the camera over which walk-through pieces dither out (0 = off). Vegetation look A (docs/architecture.md 'Rendering'): `castle_foliage` (every tree and hedge) is the one row whose step is wider than the 0.06 cap (softness 0.14, an approved exception for foliage, docs/art/style-guide.md section 12): with the crowns' normals bent away from their centres it draws two or three soft bands across a crown; its shadows are a cool blue-green. A row with shadeShift > 0, aoFloor < 1 or valueFloor < 1 reads COLOR_0 as shade instead of multiplying the albedo by it. `post.ssao` = the High-only screen-space AO's look (tint = the multiplier at full occlusion, a mauve, never grey; strength; radius m; fadeEnd m; characters = strength share on character pixels).",
