  "outline": {
    "_doc": "Character outlines, Genshin style (client/src/game/toon/outline.ts; docs/art/character-look.md section 4): an inverted hull, a second skinned draw of each near character pushed out along the baked smoothed normals (glTF _OUTLINE, tools/blender/characters/charlib/outline_bake.py, whose length is the per-vertex width weight: 0 on the face's eyes, brows, nose and mouth). width = line width in render pixels at a 1000-pixel-high frame (scaled with the render height like the old lines, 1 to 2.5 x); near/far/farScale = full width to near metres, farScale of it at far; fadeStart/fadeEnd = the line fades out (beyond, the hull is not drawn); depthPush = metres the hull sits behind the surface along the view ray (lines only past silhouettes); maxTier = the coarsest LOD tier outlined; lightRef/lightFloor = the scene's fill + key light at which the line takes its full colour, and the least light it keeps (lines darken at night with everything else). regions = per vertex region (palette.ts CHARACTER_REGIONS; 'default' for the rest), the derived rule, never a colour per character: line colour = max(pow(vertex colour, gamma) * scale * tint, floor) (the skin tone, hair colour or garment dye of that vertex, so recolours and the Chameleon Tonic recolour the line); width = multiplier (thin on the face, none on flat paint).",
