  "characters": {
    "_doc": "Character toon rows, one per vertex region (client/src/game/toon/palette.ts CHARACTER_TOON; docs/art/character-adoption.md section 5). Partial ToonRamps over BASE_RAMP plus the character fields: shadeShift = how far the baked shade layer (_SHADE.x, creases 0 .. open 1) moves the key's threshold (creases fall into the tinted shadow band); aoFloor = ambient kept in the deepest crease; skyLift = hemispheric fill by normal (up-facing brighter); rimWidth = the rim's width in 1 - n.v (both bands, brighter lit); band, bandCentre, bandWidth = the hair's highlight band along _SHADE.y (root 0 .. tip 1), z its per-lock phase. Skin and face shadows warm, cloth shadows cool. The face region (the skin of the body's head) takes no shadow-map shadow and a faint rim, so faces stay clean: its shade is always open except under the fringe, whose soft shadow the client folds in at assembly, so its large shadeShift only ever moves that shadow into the band. Character look (docs/art/character-look.md section 3.4): at Medium and High the face's key light comes from the face-shadow threshold map instead (faceSdfSoftness = the step's half-width in light angle / 180), the fringe's shadow still falls into the band, and the face texture's flat paint (eyes, lashes, mouth line) is always lit. Look pass 2 (character-look.md section 3): the skin and face shadow tints are peach-rose at pass 1's brightness (the same luma); the face row's faceLineSkin = the skin luma whose painted lines (mouth, nose, lid crease) every darker skin matches in value drop, faceLineFloor = the darkest a line takes the skin (a share of it), faceIrisGlow = the share of the iris and catchlight albedo added unlit.",
